WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.020
- Hi, I'm Keke Palmer,

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.767
and I'm here to give
you some acting nopes,

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.419
and I'll throw in some yeps too.

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:07.002
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.310
Early to set is a absolute nope.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.560
I hate having to come to work early.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.393
I really do.

00:00:17.393 --> 00:00:18.630
If I do have to come early,

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.430
then I try to bring like
a blanket in the car.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.263
You know what I mean?

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:22.110
On the way, so I can try to sleep,

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:22.943
or in my trailer,

00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:23.940
I try to sleep in the makeup trailer.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.940
I try to sleep until
I have to work on set.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.620
So yeah, it's an absolute nope.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.470
(upbeat music)

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.970
Improvisation without prompting,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:33.803
it's a yep.

00:00:33.803 --> 00:00:35.940
You know, I mean, I, I
definitely prefer to know

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.370
if somebody wants me to do
improv because I actually

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.620
really respect, you know,
obviously a writer's word.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.650
So I don't wanna add to it
if it shouldn't be added to,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.660
but I do love to improv
and I can have fun,

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.520
but I just like to get
the signal that it's cool

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.794
so I don't disrespect
the words on the page.

00:00:49.794 --> 00:00:53.040
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.390
Oh, nope, no, you do not
disobey what the animal

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.320
trainer has said.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.310
Absolutely not.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.143
Yeah.

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:02.700
When that happened in the
movie, I'm like, mm-mm girl, no,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.720
that's why you can't do that.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.180
You have to really be, you
know, respectful of their job

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.070
because they know these
animals and they know how

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.420
the animals want to be approached.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.160
You cannot disrespect
them and, and what they're

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.260
doin' because that's when things go wrong.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.080
So yeah, I definitely always
take my lead from the animal

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.640
wranglers and know what I need to do

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.283
when I don't need to do it.

00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:22.290
(calming music)

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.110
Ignoring continuity is a absolute nope.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.790
Okay, I come from the
old school where yes,

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.260
I let the prop people do they job,

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.520
I let everybody do their resets,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.430
but it's to the point where
I will self reset as well

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.410
because I really take pride in continuity

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.243
and things like that,

00:01:35.243 --> 00:01:37.590
it's one of the first
things I learned on set.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.260
I did a movie with William
H. Macy, called The Wool Cap,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.300
when I was 10, in Montreal.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.520
And, I remember, you know, I
was like, what are you doin'

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.620
askin' the people that kept
bringing everything back?

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.450
And they said, this is
continuity, you know,

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.490
and they explained to me
Scripty and all that stuff.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.280
And so, ever since then, I
always took such pride in it.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.066
So yeah, you gotta pay attention.

00:01:55.066 --> 00:01:58.200
(upbeat music)

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.470
Only being sorta off
book is a absolute nope.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.310
Okay?

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.280
The only thing I'm sorta on
is, like, the performance

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.620
that I'm gonna choose, but
you've gotta know those lines

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.590
if you expect to do a
performance or have a,

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.390
have a collaboration
with the director on what

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.280
the performance could or
couldn't be, you know,

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.350
you have to know the lines
'cuz if you don't know

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.820
the lines then how you gonna play with it?

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:18.720
You know, you gonna be too busy

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.190
worried about what the
lines are, you know?

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.260
And I don't wanna hold up our whole crew,

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.820
have everybody there for hours and hours

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.260
'cause I didn't study my
lines the night before,

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.180
that's crazy.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.370
(upbeat music)

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.470
Makin' friends with
Crafty is absolute yup.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.340
Yeah, like why not?

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.180
You know what I mean?

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.380
Especially if you guys like end up

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.280
really gettin' to know each other

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.050
then they can give you
like some special treats,

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.790
special little sandwiches, you know.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.623
But yeah, it's great.

00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:43.719
I mean Crafty is like the
unsung hero on every set.

00:02:43.719 --> 00:02:46.302
(upbeat music)

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.510
Phoning in anything on
set is a absolute nope.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.830
You cannot do this.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:53.663
You cannot do this.

00:02:53.663 --> 00:02:54.600
No, no, no.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.120
Because it's like marking a dance step,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.470
if you mark it the whole way,

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.880
then when it's time to really perform

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.290
you're gonna be marking it.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.030
So, you know, you can't phone it in.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.340
Now, yes, you don't
wanna tire yourself out,

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.920
but you have to be true
to it at least a couple

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.870
of times with your director
so you guys can really

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.920
get into the vibe of it,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.990
and then if you need to take
a break 'cuz you don't wanna

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.540
overuse your muscle in that
moment, that's understandable,

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.340
but phoning it in totally,

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.270
no, no, no.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.843
I'm Keke Palmer and this
has been Acting Nopes.

